14. We note the finding of an apparent association between the use of the beaches in the proximity of Dounreay by children and the development of leukaemia/NHL. We advise that this finding should be interpreted with considerable caution since:



14.1
it relates to five cases only;


14.2
it is based on parental recall some years after the event which may be subject to human error;


14.3
the only comparable study [3] did not produce a similar result;


14.4
information, currently available, on the levels of radioactivity on the beaches, suggests that these are far too low to cause leukaemia on the basis of accepted models of leukaemogenesis.

Mr. Curry: Several changes have been introduced for the third year of the set-aside scheme in particular to improve its impact upon the environment:
The number of cuts required of the plant cover on fallow set-aside land has been increased from one to two;
The list of environmental features which farmers have to maintain and protect on set-aside land has been extended;
A limited grazed fallow option has been included;
The rates of aid for permanent and rotational fallow have been increased, partly to offset the increased costs arising from the new management rules;
Differential rates of aid have been introduced for farmers who fallow more than 100 hectares of land and more than 75 per cent. of their eligible area, in order to reflect better the fixed cost savings.

